{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\( x \\) in the determinant equation\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = 0,\n\\]\nwe will first compute the determinant of the given matrix. Let's denote the matrix by \\( A \\):\n\\[\nA = \\begin{pmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a - x & a + x \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the cofactor expansion along the first row to find the determinant of \\( A \\):\n\\[\n\\det(A) = (a + x) \\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} - (a - x) \\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} + (a - x) \\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\\\ a - x & a - x \\end{vmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute the 2x2 determinants:\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = (a + x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a + x)^2 - (a - x)^2 = a^2 + 2ax + x^2 - (a^2 - 2ax + x^2) = 4ax,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a - x)(a + x - (a - x)) = (a - x)(2x) = 2x(a - x),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\\\ a - x & a - x \\end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a - x) - (a + x)(a - x) = (a - x)^2 - (a + x)(a - x) = (a - x)(a - x - (a + x)) = (a - x)(-2x) = -2x(a - x).\n\\]\n\n","prefix_end":1248,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,856,1124,8,304,279,86960,23606,198,59,9640,59,7265,90,7338,2555,92,264,488,856,609,264,481,856,609,264,481,856,24984,264,481,856,609,264,488,856,609,264,481,856,24984,264,481,856,609,264,481,856,609,264,488,856,1124,408,90,7338,2555,92,284,220,15,345,59,921,896,686,1156,12564,279,86960,315,279,2661,6172,13,6771,594,78064,279,6172,553,17767,362,1124,982,59,9640,32,284,1124,7265,90,5187,2555,92,264,488,856,609,264,481,856,609,264,481,856