0.013025907799601555,-1.1920928244535389e-07,-7.152555099310121e-07,-0.018321914598345757,0.0,0.0,0.0,0.0,-0.002427014522254467,-1.2755313036905136e-05,-1.0728830375228426e-06,-9.536738616588991e-07],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,50,3948,369,400,87,3,304,198,59,26056,7265,90,7338,2555,92,264,488,856,609,264,481,856,609,264,481,856,24984,264,481,856,609,264,488,856,609,264,481,856,24984,264,481,856,609,264,481,856,609,264,488,856,1124,408,90,7338,2555,92,284,220,15,7110,60,35127,678,3204,2750,315,400,87,4779,304,3793,315,400,64,2418,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nSolve for $x$ in\n\\[\\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = 0.\\]Give all possible values of $x,$ in terms of $a.$","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"05544da9965f0b7745f7917f074705fe01d13b1f9dc5c93242dc43946f957c75"},"seconds":23.45251727104187,"seed":749221690087286907,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve for \\( x \\) in the determinant equation\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = 0,\n\\]\nwe will first compute the determinant of the given matrix. Let's denote the matrix by \\( A \\):\n\\[\nA = \\begin{pmatrix} a + x & a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a - x & a + x \\end{pmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nWe can use the cofactor expansion along the first row to find the determinant of \\( A \\):\n\\[\n\\det(A) = (a + x) \\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} - (a - x) \\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} + (a - x) \\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\\\ a - x & a - x \\end{vmatrix}.\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to compute the 2x2 determinants:\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a + x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = (a + x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a + x)^2 - (a - x)^2 = a^2 + 2ax + x^2 - (a^2 - 2ax + x^2) = 4ax,\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a - x \\\\ a - x & a + x \\end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a + x) - (a - x)(a - x) = (a - x)(a + x - (a - x)) = (a - x)(2x) = 2x(a - x),\n\\]\n\\[\n\\begin{vmatrix} a - x & a + x \\\\ a - x & a - x \\end{vmatrix} = (a - x)(a - x) - (a + x)(a - x) = (a - x)^2 - (a + x)(a - x) = (a - x)(a - x - (a + x)) = (a - x)(-2x) = -2x(a - x).\n\\]\n\nSubstituting these back into the determinant expression, we get:\n\\[\n\\det(A) = (a + x) \\cdot 4ax - (a - x) \\cdot 2x(a - x) + (a - x) \\cdot (-2x)(a - x) = 4ax(a + x) - 2x(a - x)^2 - 2x(a - x)^2 = 4ax(a + x) - 4x(a - x)^2.\n\\]\n\nFactoring out \\( 4x \\), we have:\n\\[\n\\det(A) = 4x \\left( a(a + x) - (a - x)^2 \\right) = 4x \\left( a^2 + ax - (a^2 - 2ax + x^2) \\right) = 4x \\left( a^2 + ax - a^2 + 2ax - x^2 \\right) = 4x \\left( 3ax - x^2 \\right) = 4x^2 (3a - x).\n\\]\n\nSetting the determinant equal to zero, we get:\n\\[\n4x^2 (3a - x) = 0.\n\\]\n\nThis equation is satisfied when either \\( 4x^2 = 0 \\) or \\( 3a - x = 0 \\). Solving these, we get:\n\\[\nx = 0 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x = 3a.\n\\]\n\nThus, the possible values of \\( x \\) are \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( x = 3a \\). Therefore, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{0 \\text{ and } 3a}.\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{0 \\text{ and } 3a}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"precalculus:237"}
